{
    "word": "untenanted",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "54b0f4b9-e1c6-3408-91b4-988cece9cbf3",
                "word": "untenanted",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c9c7fe79-5e03-3fad-ad6f-5bacce26ade1",
                        "entry_id": "54b0f4b9-e1c6-3408-91b4-988cece9cbf3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Not leased to or occupied by a tenant; unoccupied."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "also",
                            "figuratively",
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "06085f84-a527-45b4-b41a-ace85874a7e1",
                                "sense_id": "c9c7fe79-5e03-3fad-ad6f-5bacce26ade1",
                                "text": "As we have seen some quadrupedes formed to crop the surface of the fields, and others to live upon the tops of trees, so the Mole is formed to live wholly under the earth, as if Nature meant that no place should be left wholly untenanted."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6acd3080-8c62-43fb-8e7d-89f2a284e491",
                                "sense_id": "c9c7fe79-5e03-3fad-ad6f-5bacce26ade1",
                                "text": "[…] a throng of the revellers at once threw themselves into the black apartment, and, seizing the mummer, whose tall figure stood erect and motionless within the shadow of the ebony clock, gasped in unutterable horror at finding the grave cerements and corpse-like mask which they handled with so violent a rudeness, untenanted by any tangible form."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "11ec1202-b21c-4469-bd7b-363ebf4fe0ce",
                                "sense_id": "c9c7fe79-5e03-3fad-ad6f-5bacce26ade1",
                                "text": "The house looked as though it had been long untenanted. The windows were encrusted with dust, and the shutters were up."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3b5e8015-8317-4329-8277-6661be68cd21",
                                "sense_id": "c9c7fe79-5e03-3fad-ad6f-5bacce26ade1",
                                "text": "At five o'clock there will be few people in the broad pillared saloon, and usually the little round tables that obstruct the sidewalk before its doors are untenanted."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "537db99a-6005-4f89-8c8a-4fde7a968663",
                                "sense_id": "c9c7fe79-5e03-3fad-ad6f-5bacce26ade1",
                                "text": "Many years elapsed before the success of Kemp Town as a residential district was assured; the foundations of the estate were laid in 1823, but some houses remained untenanted until the 1850s."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "de9f92e3-9396-4c40-a0dc-b2ccc4696f8d",
                                "sense_id": "c9c7fe79-5e03-3fad-ad6f-5bacce26ade1",
                                "text": "Peter Holmes left the club and drove down to the hardware store in Elizabeth Street where he had bought the motor mower. It was untenanted and empty of people, but somebody had broken in a door and it had been partially looted in that anyone who wanted anything had just walked in to take it."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
